00:09:58.040 --> 00:09:59.970
The right to write on us currency.

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:02.520
Speaking of good or bad government,

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:05.620
let's talk about the U S
treasury, specifically money.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.150
Have you ever felt like writing on money,

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:09.670
but worried about that
pesky thing called a felony?

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:10.503
Well, don't fret,

00:10:10.503 --> 00:10:13.680
because you've got a right
to deface US currency.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:15.860
The common belief that you
can't write on or mark our bills

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:18.210
is actually a misinterpretation
of the United States Code,

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:23.210
Title 18, Part I, Chapter 17,
Section 333, which states,

00:10:24.337 --> 00:10:26.090
"Whoever mutilates, cuts,
defaces, disfigures,

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:27.660
or perforates, or unites
or cements together,

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.840
or does any other thing to
any bank bill, draft, note,

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:31.100
or other evidence of debt issued

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.450
by any national banking association,

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:34.800
or Federal Reserve Bank, or
the Federal Reserve System,

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.730
with intent to render such
bank bill, draft, note,

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:38.900
or other evidence of debt
unfit to be reissued,

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:40.690
shall be fined under
this title or imprisoned

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:42.487
by not more than six months, or both."

00:10:42.487 --> 00:10:43.840
(laughs) I did it.

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:45.530
This crime boils down to intent.

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:48.890
Did you intend to render the
bill unfit to be reissued?

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:50.930
If not, then no harm, no foul.

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:53.950
It's not as if every time
a bill has markings on it

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:55.510
it's removed from circulation.

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:58.370
So feel free to draw a
beard on Alexander Hamilton.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:00.160
It may be dumb, but you can still spend

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.432
that $100 dollar bill y'all.

00:11:02.432 --> 00:11:04.860
♪ Uh-oh, I got $100 bill y'all. ♪

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:06.260
When is a bill unfit?

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:09.030
If it's torn, dirty,
limp, worn, or defaced.

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:10.610
According to the Federal Reserve,

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:12.700
a bill is unfit if it has excessive holes,

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:15.010
tears, tape, or excessive graffiti.

00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:17.770
So a black eye on George
Washington is probably okay,

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:20.840
but a torn in half bill is probably not,

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:21.750
not that there's any reason

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:23.370
why you should be tearing
up your own money.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.127
Money's better when you can spend it,

00:11:25.127 --> 00:11:26.850
#NotLegalAdvice,

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:29.030
#CommonSense.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:30.900
The right to give your children alcohol.

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:33.650
Philosopher, William Smith,
famously observed that.

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:35.400
- Parents just don't understand.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.870
- But just because Carlton, Aunt Viv,

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:37.830
and Uncle Phil were square,

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.630
doesn't mean that all parents are narcs.

